  "allow_event_aligned_direct_positive_without_level": true,
  "constraints": [
    "This is a new shadow policy and does not overwrite frozen v1.",
    "The final report is emitted once as Picked, Possible, Fallback-Possible, or Context.",
    "Clinical decision fields remain immutable; final reporting roles do not create formal causal claims.",
    "Reads remain per-test evidence and are never summed across DNA, RNA, or technical repeats.",
    "Missing PCR, beta-D-glucan, culture, viral load, history, or timing is unknown and never negative.",
    "Recorded but dose-unverified immunosuppressive exposure may support PJP Possible but cannot create Picked.",
    "Explicit current reactivation reduces incidental-reactivation concern; absence of such wording does not prove no reactivation.",
    "Strong cross-molecule repeated evidence may create Possible despite taxonomy source caution but not Picked.",
    "An aspiration-family candidate already moved from Context to Priority by the frozen history route may enter Possible only with complete, reproducible cross-molecule mNGS evidence; consumed history is not reused to create Picked.",
    "Analytical-only candidates remain visible in Context when every positive test is fully evaluable, every test has RPM, and all per-test RPM values remain below the fixed burden threshold; test count itself never causes demotion.",
    "Analytical-only candidates whose family is genus-inherited require recorded host context to remain in the primary report.",
    "Fallback runs only when a patient has no Picked or Possible and is visibly labeled low-confidence best available.",
    "The policy is answer blind; benchmark answers are used only by a separate post-hoc evaluator."
  ]
}
